+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool calls are checked against the schema declared by the resolved tool definition before an executor receives them.
+
+- A call missing a required property returns a descriptive tool result and does not invoke the executor. ([validated by: rejects a missing required property before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10))
+- A value with the wrong declared type returns a message naming the property and expected type without exposing the offending value. ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed value without exposing it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28))
+- After a rejected call, valid input containing an undeclared extra property reaches the executor unchanged exactly once. ([validated by: passes valid input and extra properties through unchanged after rejecting invalid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L44))
+- A static tool schema that cannot be compiled fails registration and names the tool. ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema during registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L65))
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each call, so each call is validated against its current schema. ([validated by: validates function-valued definitions against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L73))
